WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.100
- All right. Jennell?

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:06.933
Jennell.

00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:08.071
Where'd you grow up? Where
are you from, originally?

00:00:08.071 --> 00:00:09.650
- Seward, Alaska.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:10.920
- Alaska?
- Yup.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.190
- And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.710
You had both your parents as a kid?

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.370
- Um, well, not really.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.900
I had my mom and my grandparents.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.793
My dad was out of the picture
by the time I was six.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.090
- How would you describe your childhood?

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.790
- My childhood was really good.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.440
I was raised with horses

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.793
and I did a lot of dancing
and gymnastics and swimming.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.000
And then my mom met my stepdad

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.370
and pulled us away from all of that

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.630
and moved us to Anchorage.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.660
And I did not like that.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.110
I didn't like that at all.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.940
And I left home at 13,

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.773
after that.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.380
We did some ballroom dancing before that

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.080
you know, ballroom and
Latin dancing and stuff.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.180
And it wasn't my thing.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.880
- So what was going on that
made you leave home at 13?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.580
- I was really upset they
took me away from my horses,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.010
in Fairbanks.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.660
So, then I got into the drugs

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.010
with all the kids at school,

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.410
you know, started with pot and then acid.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.170
Then I left home with my boyfriend

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.570
and that's when everything
went really bad.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.160
- How was growing up in Alaska? Is it--

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:15.993
- Cold.

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:16.826
Really cold?

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:18.350
- I'm sure it's cold, but is it?

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.660
Are there, are drugs
pretty common down there?

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.550
- That's all there is to do.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.290
That's all there is to do.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.580
There's nothing else to do.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.830
- Mm.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:27.663
- So--

00:01:27.663 --> 00:01:29.590
- And your boyfriend went where?

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.100
- Oh, on the street.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.410
His mom was a, um,

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.230
a crack whore

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.880
and she real quickly turned me out.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.040
So by the time I was 13

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.480
I was prostituting

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.727
and using crack cocaine.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:43.560
- Mm.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.893
- And then from there I was,

00:01:48.804 --> 00:01:51.690
I prostituted 'til I was 21.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.633
And then,

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.660
on and off the streets

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.200
and, I don't know,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.330
life, life has just been hard.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.433
Like when I was eight, I was
molested by my Camp Counselor.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.180
And,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.890
I don't remember that though.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.417
I've just been told about it

00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:10.820
but I guess it was pretty bad,

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:11.990
but, um,

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.010
I don't know, I've just
been on and off the streets

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.410
since, since then.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:16.540
- Did you finish school?

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:17.373
- No.

00:02:17.373 --> 00:02:18.560
- How far did you go?

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.250
- Eighth, ninth grade.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.000
Two weeks into my ninth grade year.

00:02:23.798 --> 00:02:25.210
- And today your how old?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.043
- I'm 44.

00:02:26.043 --> 00:02:26.876
- 44.

00:02:26.876 --> 00:02:27.900
Do you have kids?

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.910
- Yeah. I have three daughters.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.790
- And where are they?

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.063
- They're in Fairbanks.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.930
- Who's raising them?

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.390
- They're all grown, all
except for my youngest.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.500
She's 15.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.423
Her dad has her.

00:02:40.508 --> 00:02:42.173
- And so did you raise your kids?

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:43.963
- Um, no.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.820
No. My two oldest were
raised by my grandparents

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.653
and

00:02:50.653 --> 00:02:51.660
my mom

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.003
and my youngest was
between me and her dad.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.410
- So prostitution was the
way you were surviving

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.243
for--

00:03:01.243 --> 00:03:02.560
- For a long time.
- For a long time?

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.816
- I still do once in a while. Yeah.

00:03:04.816 --> 00:03:07.410
- Yeah. So today you're in Skid Row?

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.243
- Yeah.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.242
- And how? You're still
using drugs, I take it?

00:03:13.242 --> 00:03:14.075
- Yeah.

00:03:14.075 --> 00:03:15.180
- What's your drug today?

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.013
- Heroin.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.980
- And this is rough life as well, right?

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.170
- Oh, yeah, too rough.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.450
- Is it rougher here in
Skid Row than, than--

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.400
- No.
- Alaska?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.820
- No. This is way easier, way easier.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.653
- The weather's easy?

00:03:29.653 --> 00:03:31.513
- Yeah. It's not 60 below zero.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.000
So this is kinda nice, actually.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:35.953
It's a nice change.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.600
- And how long have you been here?

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.433
- Two weeks.

00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:40.266
- Oh, you're brand new?

00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:41.340
- Yeah.
- From where?

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.173
- From Fairbanks.

00:03:42.173 --> 00:03:43.150
- Oh, from Alaska.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.100
- Yeah.
- Oh, wow.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.030
- I had never been out of Alaska until now

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.218
- So LA must be a nice, nice breakthrough

00:03:49.218 --> 00:03:52.120
- It's a wonderful change.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.800
- It's dangerous here too as well though?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.650
- Yeah.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.510
Yeah.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.773
I've had a couple scares,

00:03:58.621 --> 00:03:59.454
but...

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.123
- So tell, tell me what
happened between those years.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.283
So in your 30's and 40's,
you were doing what?

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.374
- Well I actually was doing okay

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:10.580
in my 30's and 40's

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.820
I bought a piece of property

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:13.990
and, um,

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.230
owned a home.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.332
It burned down.

00:04:16.332 --> 00:04:17.969
- How did you afford to buy a home?

00:04:17.969 --> 00:04:21.090
- Um, I only had to pay
8,000 for the property.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.910
So I worked a little
bit with my grandparents

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.860
and some other things to make the money

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.020
and bought the property, put
a double wide trailer on there

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.110
and ended up getting pregnant,

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.490
having my daughter.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.000
And three days after
we moved into the home

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.440
it burned down with us in it.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.053
And so that was pretty scary,

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:46.550
but we, we got out, thank God,

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.650
barely, but we got out

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.580
and then we put another trailer up

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.413
and,

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.790
I have been struggling to survive there

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.623
up until now.

00:04:56.623 --> 00:04:57.650
And I just, I couldn't do it no more

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.383
so I sold the place and left.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.150
- So if you could put
your finger on one thing

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.970
that kinda led to your

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.552
spiraling downward--

00:05:05.552 --> 00:05:06.550
- Drugs.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.950
- Drugs?
- All the way.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.870
- Not, not the molestation
when you were young.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.600
- Oh, that could be it,

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.290
I just don't remember it.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.400
I've been told about it by several people.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.400
I've, I've seen the paperwork.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.770
I'm the only one out of
22 kids that testified.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.930
And, um,

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.810
I guess it took a couple years.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.660
I remember, I remember the court

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.610
going, going to see the
judges and everything.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.810
There was like 12 judges around the table

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:32.950
that I had to sit there in front of

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.910
with a doll and tell them what happened.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.610
I don't remember what I told them.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:39.000
I do remember leaving.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.070
And my lawyer gave me a kitten

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.003
but that's about all I remember of that.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.670
- A horrible thing.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.420
- Yeah. The paperwork
said it was pretty bad

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.430
mm, it was really bad.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.630
- And do you still have
contact with your family?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.463
- Yeah.

00:05:56.463 --> 00:05:57.296
- Your kids?
- Yeah.

00:05:57.296 --> 00:05:58.129
- Yeah.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.220
- Yeah. My middle daughter
doesn't like me too much

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.830
but,

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.430
my other kids like me all right.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.660
- And wait, what's the worst
part of this lifestyle for you?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.640
Living on the street,

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.518
drugs, prostitution, all that.

00:06:11.518 --> 00:06:13.140
- Not being with my kids.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:13.973
- Yeah.

00:06:17.705 --> 00:06:20.120
- Having to struggle all the time.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.040
- Did you have dreams as a kid

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.140
of doing something with your life?

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:23.730
- Oh, yeah.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.400
Yeah. I wanted to be, I
don't want it to be anything.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.840
I thought I was gonna be a
professional horseback rider

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.357
you know, just horses and stuff like that.

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:33.900
But it didn't go that way.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:34.733
- Yeah.

00:06:35.673 --> 00:06:37.650
And do you have friends?

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.483
- Oh yeah.

00:06:38.483 --> 00:06:39.370
I've got lots of friends,

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.053
but none of them any good.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.010
- You ever been in love?

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.523
- Oh, yeah. Too many times.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:50.850
In fact, I'm trying to

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:55.780
I guess I'm in a
relationship still Fairbanks

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.400
kind of, he thinks I'm coming back.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.950
I'm not,

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.400
so

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.760
that's hard.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.710
That's really hard.

00:07:05.018 --> 00:07:06.730
- And what do you worry about?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.660
- What do I worry about?

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.077
Surviving another day?

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.313
It's hard out here.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.290
- Do you see that the
family you grew up in

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.650
might've

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.860
set the path for this

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.760
all that happened?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.020
Or your family was pretty solid?

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.200
- Well, they were, when I was younger

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.180
and then they got really weird

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.250
and everything just really fell apart

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.020
when my mom took us away
from my grandparents

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.380
and fell apart really bad.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.300
My grandparents really turned out to be

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.550
not who they were.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:51.500
I mean, they're mean, they're
extremely mean and nasty now

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.266
to the grandkids.

00:07:53.266 --> 00:07:54.837
- Some, something must've
been off for a 13 year old

00:07:54.837 --> 00:07:56.690
to go out in the street.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:57.523
- Yeah.

00:07:57.523 --> 00:07:59.110
- And not finish school.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:01.670
- I absolutely hated the fact

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.840
that my mom took me away from my horses.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.810
I hated her for that.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:06.643
I still do.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.080
I don't hate her for it, but

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.003
I definitely am still pissed.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.740
- And how do you feel all
these years on the street

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.280
and doing questionable things for money

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.113
has changed you?

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.870
- It's turned me into a
lot harder of a person.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.883
I'm not nearly as nice
as I probably could be.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:29.637
I don't trust anybody anymore.

00:08:29.637 --> 00:08:31.340
- Trust, trust must be a big issue, right?

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.385
- Yeah.

00:08:32.385 --> 00:08:33.218
It's a huge issue.

00:08:33.218 --> 00:08:34.580
- So you think everyone
down here is a snake?

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.413
- Yeah.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.540
I get sick of being groped constantly

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.093
by the men down here, you know,

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:44.494
it's irritating.

00:08:44.494 --> 00:08:45.327
- Right.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.410
But you still have hope for your future?

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.253
- Not really.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.700
Now I'm pretty much guessing

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.300
this is about how it's gonna be.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.083
I don't see much else happening.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:06.380
I'm a little too old to

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.330
come up at all

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:14.000
I feel, I don't see any big
sums of money happening,

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.488
you know? So--

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:17.238
- What, what was your lowest point?

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.430
- My lowest point?

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:20.743
It's probably right now.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.503
Being down here with absolutely nothing.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:26.720
No car,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.170
no home.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.283
Just my sister.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.240
It's hard.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.090
No money,

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.080
no food,

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:34.913
no nothing.

00:09:38.194 --> 00:09:40.940
- And what's the most important
lesson you've learned?

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.843
- Stay the fuck away from drugs.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.590
I wish I could get away from them.

00:09:48.549 --> 00:09:50.240
I hate 'em.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.073
- Tell me about Alaska.

00:09:51.073 --> 00:09:52.060
I mean, it seems like

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.140
that must be a, a rough--

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.660
- It's cold there.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.560
It's really, really cold.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.710
If you don't have a place
to live, you're screwed.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:03.340
There's no way you can
live on the streets there.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:06.400
You have to either couch
hop or go to a shelter.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:09.140
If there's an available bed,

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.570
if not you're living in your car

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:12.840
and you better hope you have gas,

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.000
'cause if not you're gonna freeze to death

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.400
in the winter anyway.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.233
- Lit, literally?

00:10:17.233 --> 00:10:18.066
- Yeah. Literally.

00:10:18.066 --> 00:10:18.899
- Yeah.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.043
- 60 below zero is no joke.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.840
- What, what do you think was the,

00:10:30.114 --> 00:10:32.520
the, the basis of your mom's,

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.353
what you think, do you

00:10:33.353 --> 00:10:35.120
do you see your mom is just being selfish

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.200
in taking you away from what you loved?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.570
- Well, she was addicted
to drugs really bad

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.440
when I was younger.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:41.620
- Oh, she was an addict as well?

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.230
- Yeah. And then she got
clean and met my stepdad

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.820
and my stepdad swept her off her feet

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:51.510
and he what he said went and
he wanted to move to Anchorage.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.810
And so that's what we did.

00:10:55.684 --> 00:10:57.690
And I wasn't very happy with that at all.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.523
- Yeah.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.173
And heroin down here,

00:11:05.173 --> 00:11:09.630
I mean, the quality of it is
probably questionable. Right?

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.300
- It's not very good.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:14.210
now I have to say the stuff
in Fairbanks is better

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.063
by far,

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:16.863
which is strange.

00:11:16.863 --> 00:11:17.840
I thought it would be better here.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:18.693
It's not though.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:20.563
Not at all.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.440
- And where do you see your life going?

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.390
I mean, you've already mentioned

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:32.760
that maybe you're stuck
in this will be it.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.020
- Yeah. I hope not.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.070
I mean, I, I'm hoping

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.540
I'm hoping I just got
accepted for the unemployment

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.620
so I'm hoping maybe I can get an apartment

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.910
or something like that, but I don't know.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.373
And then maybe find a job.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.730
I don't know,

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.610
with this COVID thing, who knows?

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:51.700
- Yeah.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.060
- It's kinda screwing everything up.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.450
- And is, does that affect your work

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.050
if you're dating guys that must--

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:58.883
- Big time,

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:00.623
big time.

00:12:00.623 --> 00:12:03.000
- 'Cause you fear potential
clients out there?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.832
- Yeah. Then a lot of
calls quit coming in.

00:12:05.832 --> 00:12:07.620
And there's a lot of
people that are scared.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:08.453
- Yeah.

00:12:08.453 --> 00:12:11.710
- So, yeah. Not very much
money in it right now.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.670
- Yeah. Everyone's scrambling for

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.503
a buck right now.

00:12:14.503 --> 00:12:15.336
- Yeah.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.250
- All right, Jannell,
well thank you so much

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.437
for sharing your story.
- Yeah.

00:12:19.437 --> 00:12:20.930
- And I wish you the best of luck.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.250
- Thank you.
- Welcome to LA.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.240
- Thanks.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.073
- Welcome to hell.

00:12:24.073 --> 00:12:25.435
- Yeah.

00:12:25.435 --> 00:12:27.268
- We're in Skid Row's.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.623
- Yeah, it definitely is.

